        "original_id": "12fa8cc6-af4e-5728-9e61-c56891c4ce6a",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Benny Andersson, Björn Ulvaeus\n- Groups: ABBA\n- Songs: \"Money, Money, Money\", \"That's Me\", \"She's My Kind of Girl\"\n- Albums: \"Arrival\"\n- Musicals: \"Chess\", \"Kristina från Duvemåla\", \"Mamma Mia!\"\n- Places: Japan\n\nFacts:\n- Benny Andersson was born on 16 December 1946.\n- Benny Andersson is a Swedish musician and composer.\n- Benny Andersson was a member of ABBA from 1972 to 1982.\n- Benny Andersson and Björn Ulvaeus wrote the song \"Money, Money, Money\" for ABBA.\n- Benny Andersson and Björn Ulvaeus wrote and performed the song \"She's My Kind of Girl\" before they became famous as members of ABBA.\n- The song \"That's Me\" was released as a single in Japan the year after its original release with \"Money, Money, Money\" as its B-side.\n- The song \"That's Me\" was released in Japan to promote ABBA's album \"Arrival\".\n- The song \"That's Me\" reached number 75 on the official Japanese charts.\n- Benny Andersson co-composed the musicals \"Chess\", \"Kristina från Duvemåla\", and \"Mamma Mia!\".",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
